# MonARCH — seed-only files
#
# Paths listed here are installed by monarch-config-apply when they are MISSING
# and are never touched again: not overwritten, not backed up, not compared.
#
# Two kinds of file belong here:
#
#   yours       settings and monitor layout. An update that resets these is a
#               bug, not a feature.
#   generated   written by another part of MonARCH (the theme engine, the
#               keybind generator). Re-deploying the repo's copy over a
#               generated file would silently undo `monarch theme apply`.
#
# Paths are relative to config/ and matched with bash glob rules, so a trailing
# /* covers a directory.

# Yours.
monarch/settings.toml
hypr/monitors.conf

# Generated by `monarch theme apply`. Kept as a guard, not because anything
# matches it today: since T3 the palette files under monarch/theme/ are not
# shipped at all — install/30-config.sh renders them from themes/_templates
# instead, so there is exactly one producer of a colour and no checked-in copy
# to drift away from it. If a file ever reappears in config/monarch/theme/,
# this line stops an update from overwriting an applied theme with it.
monarch/theme/*

# btop rewrites its own config on exit, filling in every default it did not
# find. MonARCH ships it only to pin color_theme = "monarch"; an update that
# reset it would throw away every preference btop had written since.
btop/btop.conf

# Generated by `monarch keys apply` (T4). Hand-written placeholder for now.
hypr/bindings.conf

# Rewritten by `monarch startup add|remove`. Note this is autostart-USER.conf:
# autostart.conf holds the essentials, stays MonARCH's, and keeps receiving
# updates precisely because your apps are not mixed into it.
hypr/autostart-user.conf
